# Docket — every environment variable this repository reads, and where it is read.
#
# THE THING PEOPLE GET WRONG IS THE RUNTIME. Docket runs in three places and they do not share
# environment variables:
#
#   A. Vercel          the Next.js app — app/ and src/. Set in Vercel → Settings → Environment
#                      Variables. Everything here is read with process.env.
#   B. Supabase        the three Edge Functions in supabase/functions/. Set with
#      Edge Functions   `supabase secrets set --project-ref <ref> NAME=value`. Read with
#                      Deno.env.get(). A value set on Vercel is NOT visible here, and a
#                      function secret is NOT visible to the app.
#   C. Vault           two values live in the database, not in either environment above.
#      (in Postgres)   See "C." at the foot of this file.
#
# Setting a function secret on Vercel does nothing except leave a credential somewhere it is not
# needed. Setting a Vercel variable with `supabase secrets set` does the same in reverse.
#
# THE SERVICE ROLE KEY IS NEVER SET ON VERCEL. Nothing in app/ or src/ reads it and nothing ever
# may: the only Supabase clients there are supabaseServer() and supabaseBrowser(), which run as
# the signed-in person so that RLS decides. It belongs to Edge Functions and to nowhere else —
# and Supabase injects it into them for you (see B.).
#
# Every line below names the file that reads the variable. Where a variable is read nowhere, it
# says so. Nothing here is a real value.


# ============================================================ A. VERCEL (the Next.js app)

# ---- required: without these the app renders a "not configured" notice on every screen ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
#   src/lib/env.ts (supabaseUrl), src/lib/supabase/browser.ts, src/lib/csp.ts (the connect-src
#   the browser is allowed to reach), tests/e2e/smoke.spec.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#   src/lib/env.ts (supabaseAnonKey), src/lib/supabase/browser.ts. Both a JWT anon key and an
#   sb_publishable_ key work; restHeaders() in src/lib/env.ts sends each one the way it expects.

# ---- payments ----
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=
#   src/lib/providers/payments/paystack.ts, reached from src/lib/actions/booking.ts (the
#   consultation checkout) and src/lib/actions/portal.ts (paying any open invoice). Both are
#   server actions, so the key stays on the server.
#   SET THIS IN BOTH PLACES: the same key is also an Edge Function secret, because
#   supabase/functions/paystack-webhook verifies the delivery signature with it and re-verifies
#   the charge against Paystack. See B.

# ---- links in messages, and the host a firm's domain must point at ----
APP_URL=https://app.example
#   src/lib/admin-data.ts deploymentHost() — the host /admin tells a firm to point DNS at.
#   ALSO an Edge Function secret: the dispatcher prefixes it to every link it sends. See B.

# ---- web push (the public half of the VAPID pair) ----
NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
#   src/components/push/push-opt-in.tsx. The private half is a function secret and never
#   reaches a browser.

# ---- video ----
DAILY_DOMAIN=
#   next.config.mjs, at BUILD time. It names the exact room origin in Permissions-Policy so the
#   consultation iframe may use the camera, the microphone and screen share. Left unset, that
#   policy falls back to '*' for those three features — which still works, but is wider than it
#   needs to be. Either "yourteam" or "yourteam.daily.co" is accepted.
#   Because it is read at build time, changing it needs a redeploy, not just a restart.

# ---- custom domains (the /admin domain controls) ----
VERCEL_TOKEN=
VERCEL_PROJECT_ID=
VERCEL_TEAM_ID=
#   src/lib/providers/domains/vercel.ts, reached from app/admin/actions.ts. VERCEL_TOKEN needs
#   write access to the project's domains. With TOKEN or PROJECT_ID missing, /admin says so and
#   the domain buttons explain what is not configured rather than failing silently.
#   VERCEL_TEAM_ID is only needed when the project sits under a team.

# ---- observability (optional; each is inert when unset) ----
SENTRY_DSN=
#   src/lib/observability/sentry.ts. A DSN, not a token: https://<key>@<host>/<project>.
POSTHOG_KEY=
#   src/lib/observability/posthog.ts. Deliberately NOT NEXT_PUBLIC_: every funnel event is sent
#   from server code, there is no browser SDK and no autocapture.
POSTHOG_HOST=
#   src/lib/observability/posthog.ts. Defaults to https://eu.i.posthog.com when unset. Set it
#   for a self-hosted or US-region PostHog.

# ---- content security policy ----
CSP_REPORT_ONLY=
#   src/lib/csp.ts. Set to exactly "1" to send Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only instead of
#   the enforcing header — for finding what a new third party breaks before it breaks it.
#   Leave empty in production.

# ---- set by Vercel itself; do not add them by hand ----
#   VERCEL_ENV, VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA   src/lib/observability/sentry.ts and posthog.ts read
#                                       them to tag the environment and the release.
#   NODE_ENV                            src/lib/csp.ts, sentry.ts, posthog.ts.


# ============================================================ B. SUPABASE EDGE FUNCTION SECRETS
#
#   supabase secrets set --project-ref <ref> NAME=value
#
# These are NOT Vercel variables. Every one is read with Deno.env.get() inside
# supabase/functions/.
#
# Injected by Supabase into every function — never set these yourself:
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY.
#   Read by all three functions; the service role is used there and nowhere else.

# ---- supabase/functions/paystack-webhook ----
# PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=
#   Verifies x-paystack-signature (HMAC-SHA512 of the raw body) and re-verifies the charge at
#   /transaction/verify before record_payment() sees a figure. Must be the SAME key as the one
#   on Vercel: a checkout initialised with one key and a delivery signed with another will not
#   verify.

# ---- supabase/functions/video-session ----
# DAILY_API_KEY=
#   The only place rooms and owner tokens are minted. The app never talks to Daily directly.

# ---- supabase/functions/dispatch-notifications ----
# CRON_SECRET=
#   The ONLY credential on this function (it is deployed with --no-verify-jwt). pg_cron sends it
#   as x-cron-secret and the function compares digests, not strings. The same value goes into
#   Vault as `cron_secret` — see C.
# APP_URL=
#   Prefixed to every link in an email, SMS or push message.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# EMAIL_FROM=notifications@example
#   Email. EMAIL_FROM must be a sender Resend has verified for the domain.
# TERMII_API_KEY=
# TERMII_SENDER_ID=
#   SMS to Nigerian numbers (+234), sent on the DND route. TERMII_SENDER_ID defaults to "Docket"
#   in the function when unset; use a sender ID Termii has approved.
# TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# TWILIO_FROM=
#   SMS to every other country code.
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
# VAPID_SUBJECT=mailto:ops@example
#   Web push. VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY must be the same key as NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY on Vercel —
#   a subscription made with one public key cannot be signed with another. VAPID_SUBJECT
#   defaults to mailto:ops@docket.app in the function when unset.


# ============================================================ C. VAULT (inside the database)
#
# Not environment variables at all. Migration 9 schedules `docket-dispatch-notifications` in
# pg_cron, and that job reads two secrets out of Vault every minute. Until BOTH exist the job
# runs and posts nothing, so no message is ever sent.
#
#   select vault.create_secret('https://<ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/dispatch-notifications',
#                              'dispatch_url');
#   select vault.create_secret('<the same CRON_SECRET as above>', 'cron_secret');


# ============================================================ D. LOCAL SHELL AND CI ONLY
#
# Never set on Vercel and never a function secret.

DATABASE_URL=
#   scripts/db-test-local.sh. A LOCAL Postgres 16 superuser connection: the suite creates roles
#   and an auth schema, and it drops and recreates a database called docket_test. Give it a bare
#   URL with no query string — the script takes everything before the final slash.
#   Never point this at a Supabase project.

PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL=
#   playwright.config.ts. Point the smoke tests at a deployment; unset, the config starts
#   `next dev` on http://localhost:3000 itself.

E2E_FIRM_SLUG=
#   tests/e2e/smoke.spec.ts, for the one test that opens a tenant's public home. The fallback in
#   that file is a single named firm's slug, so set this to a slug that exists in the deployment
#   you are testing.

# scripts/configure-providers.sh reads these, and only from the shell you run it in:
#   SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN       a personal access token (supabase.com/dashboard/account/tokens)
#   SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF        the project ref
#   APP_URL                     the production origin, for the Auth Site URL and allow-list
#   EXTRA_REDIRECT_URLS         optional, comma-separated (preview deployments)
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_MESSAGE_SERVICE_SID
#                               all three together enable Supabase Auth's own SMS OTP provider.
#                               Note TWILIO_MESSAGE_SERVICE_SID is used ONLY by this script;
#                               the dispatcher uses TWILIO_FROM instead.


# ============================================================ E. DEAD — read by nothing
#
# Listed so nobody sets them expecting an effect. Delete them from any environment they are in.
#
#   PAYSTACK_PUBLIC_KEY   Nothing reads it. Docket never mounts Paystack's browser SDK: the
#                         checkout is a server-side initialise and a redirect.
#   SUPABASE_URL          on Vercel. app/ and src/ read only the NEXT_PUBLIC_ pair. Inside Edge
#   SUPABASE_ANON_KEY     Functions these two are live, and Supabase provides them.
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY
#                         on Vercel. It must never be set there.
#   DAILY_API_KEY         on Vercel. src/lib/providers/video/daily.ts reads it, but nothing in
#                         app/ or src/ imports that module — the video-session Edge Function
#                         does all of it. Function secret only.
#   RESEND_API_KEY, EMAIL_FROM, TERMII_API_KEY, TERMII_SENDER_ID,
#   TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID, TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN, TWILIO_FROM
#                         on Vercel. src/lib/providers/messaging/* reads them and nothing in
#                         app/ or src/ imports it — the dispatcher Edge Function sends every
#                         message. Function secrets only.
